# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Subject rules:
#   - Imperative mood ("add", "fix", "remove" — not "added"/"adds")
#   - <= 72 characters
#   - No trailing period
#   - Lowercase after the colon, except for proper nouns
#
# Allowed types:
#   feat     - new user-visible capability
#   fix      - bug fix
#   refactor - internal change with no behavior change
#   perf     - performance improvement
#   docs     - documentation only
#   test     - tests only
#   chore    - build, deps, tooling, repo cleanup
#   ci       - CI/CD changes
#   build    - build system changes
#   style    - formatting only, no logic
#
# Scope is optional but encouraged: e.g. hooks, cli, sync, providers, server
#
# Body (optional, separate with a blank line):
#   - Explain the WHY, not the WHAT. The diff says what.
#   - Wrap at 72 chars.
#   - Reference Beads issue if non-trivial: "Refs: construct-XXX".
#
# Footer (optional):
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description of breaking change>
#   Refs: construct-XXX, #123
#
# Forbidden:
#   - "Co-Authored-By: Claude*" lines unless the user explicitly asks
#   - Itemized feature lists in the body (the diff already shows them)
#   - --no-verify or --no-gpg-sign without explicit user authorization
